 child cannot be used to work backwards to its parent.', '#0f6b45'],\n    ['Release child', 'action', 'promote to focused secret', 'Every lens then points at the child instead of the parent.', '#0f6b45']\n  ],\n  qr: [\n    ['Format', 'SeedQR', 'Standard · 21 × 21 · version 1', 'Compact and Address QR are the other two modes.', '#5c5344'],\n    ['Contents', 'plaintext seed', 'the entire 24-word phrase', 'Anyone who photographs this can spend from the wallet.', '#b3261e'],\n    ['Acknowledge', 'required', 'checked', 'Generation stays blocked until this is checked.', '#0f6b45'],\n    ['Printer warning', 'read it', 'queues · memory · cloud sync retain copies', 'Print from an offline machine, or transcribe by hand.', '#b3261e'],\n    ['Device transfer', 'ADR-26', 'animated QR · live only', 'Nothing downloadable, and the receiver still types the vault phrase.', '#0f6b45'],\n    ['Address QR', 'public', 'safe to share and photograph', 'A receive address in a QR is not a secret.', '#0f6b45']\n  ],\n  conceal: [\n    ['Re-enter phrase', 'required', '•••••••••••••••••', 'The same phrase that unlocked this vault. It does not cross back to warm.', '#5c5344'],\n    ['Wallet · Travel set', 'hidden', 'out of lists and search', '', '#8a6100'],\n    ['Note · Where the plates are', 'hidden', 'out of lists and search', '', '#8a6100'],\n    ['Device · Trezor One', 'hidden', 'retired', '', '#8a6100'],\n    ['Secret notes', 'always cold', 'never enters the warm shell', 'A different mechanism entirely — not affected by revealing.', '#0f6b45'],\n    ['What hiding is not', 'read it', 'not a second vault', 'Reversible tidiness and shoulder-surfing defence. The compartment was already encrypted.', '#b3261e']\n  ],\n  validate: [\n    ['Words in wordlist', 'spelling', '23 of 24', 'Word 17 reads “jungel”, which is not a BIP-39 word.', '#b3261e'],\n    ['Checksum', 'not reported', 'cannot check yet', 'A guessed word would produce a meaningless verdict, so nothing is guessed.', '#8a6100'],\n    ['Wordlist', 'detected', 'English · 2048 words', 'Ten wordlists are vendored and covered by official vectors.', '#5c5344'],\n    ['Fingerprint', 'blocked', 'not calculated', 'Appears once every word resolves and the checksum agrees.', '#5c5344'],\n    ['Passphrase pair', 'confirmed', 'match', 'A passphrase makes a different wallet from the same words.', '#0f6b45'],\n    ['Release', 'disabled', 'fix the phrase first', 'Release needs both verdicts green.', '#b3261e']\n  ],\n  backuphealth: [\n    ['Worst case today', 'scored', 'one lost share is survivable', 'A 3-of-5 set with shares in five places.', '#0f6b45'],\n    ['SLIP-39 3-of-5', 'unverified', 'scores as NO backup', 'You have never reconstructed it. Until you do, it is an assumption.', '#b3261e'],\n    ['Seed XOR 4 parts', 'no threshold', 'every part required', 'Lose one part and the wallet is gone.', '#b3261e'],\n    ['Passphrase', 'separate secret', 'not covered by any share set', 'Back it up separately or the shares are useless.', '#b3261e'],\n    ['Device spread', 'ok', '3 devices · 3 locations', 'No two keys in the same building.', '#0f6b45'],\n    ['Next action', 'do this', 'reconstruct the 3-of-5 set', 'Combine · recover in Split lab, then mark verified.', '#0f6b45']\n  ],\n  verifyfile: [\n    ['Drop the file', 'tap to choose', 'coldbox-1.0.0.html', 'Hashed in your browser. Nothing is uploaded — cold has no network at all.', '#5c5344'],\n    ['SHA-256', 'computed', '9f2c41a7e0d5b93c6417ff08a2d9e1b7', 'Compare every character against the published value.', '#0f6b45'],\n    ['Published hash', 'from the release', '9f2c41a7e0d5b93c6417ff08a2d9e1b7', 'match', '#0f6b45'],\n    ['Verdict', 'match', 'the bytes are the published bytes', 'This proves the file was not altered. It does not prove the code is trustworthy.', '#0f6b45'],\n    ['Signature', 'separate step', 'verify with your own tool', 'A hash match with a forged published hash proves nothing.', '#8a6100'],\n    ['Provenance', 'P0.16', 'build id · commit · date', 'Recorded in the file itself so it can be checked offline.', '#5c5344']\n  ],\n  devices: [\n    ['Trezor Model T', 'fw 2.8.7 · current', '3A9F2C41 · Steel plate', 'SLIP-39 capable. Fingerprint verified 11 Aug.', '#0f6b45'],\n    ['Coldcard Mk4', 'fw 5.3.3 · update', 'B71E0D5A · Multisig key 2', 'Seed XOR capable. SLIP-39 not supported.', '#8a6100'],\n    ['Ledger Nano S+', 'fw 1.1.2 · current', '6C24FF08 · Daily spend', 'SLIP-39 not supported. Passphrase set.', '#0f6b45'],\n    ['Retired · Trezor One', 'hidden record', 'seed migrated 2024', 'Kept for history. Reveal in the sealed realm.', '#5c5344'],\n    ['Add a device', 'action', 'record · verify · label', 'Verification re-derives an address from your own xpub in cold.', '#0f6b45'],\n    ['Could you still spend?', 'answer', 'yes — 2 of 3 survive', 'Losing the Coldcard alone does not lose the multisig.', '#0f6b45']\n  ],\n  learn: [\n    ['Why not a wallet', '4 min', 'the permanent non-goal', 'Coldbox cannot sign, so compromising it cannot spend your money.', '#0f6b45'],\n    ['Two-source entropy', '6 min', 'why dice still matter', 'What protects you if the device RNG is compromised.', '#0f6b45'],\n    ['Passphrase is a second secret', '3 min', 'and it needs its own backup', 'No share scheme on the Split lab page covers it.', '#b3261e'],\n    ['Threshold vs all-parts', '5 min', 'SLIP-39 against Seed XOR', 'Which failure you are choosing when you pick a scheme.', '#0f6b45'],\n    ['Verify, do not trust', '4 min', 'addresses and firmware', 'How address-swapping malware actually gets caught.', '#0f6b45'],\n    ['A backup you never tested', '2 min', 'is not a backup', 'The single most common way people lose coins to themselves.', '#b3261e']\n  ],\n  dashboard: [\n    ['Warm shell', 'online ok', 'Prices · Portfolio · Registry', 'Reaches the network for public data. Never receives a secret.', '#0f6b45'],\n    ['Coldbox', 'companion', 'Holds keys: no · Signs: no · Verifies: yes', 'It cannot spend your money, so an attacker who compromises it cannot either.', '#b3261e'],\n    ['Sealed realm', 'no network', \"connect-src 'none'\", 'No fetch, no XHR, no socket. Not disabled — absent.', '#0f6b45']\n  ],\n  portfolio: [\n    ['Steel plate · savings', 'BTC · Trezor T', '0.41820000 · $18,240.00', '+$9,113.40 unrealised', '#0f6b45'],\n    ['Multisig 2-of-3 · cold', 'BTC · Coldcard', '1.05000000 · $41,900.00', '+$24,050.10 unrealised', '#0f6b45'],\n    ['Daily spend', 'BTC · Ledger S+', '0.01940000 · $1,120.00', '−$61.20 unrealised', '#b3261e'],\n    ['Contracts', 'ETH · Trezor T', '3.44100000 · $7,880.00', '+$1,204.60 unrealised', '#0f6b45']\n  ],\n  registry: [\n    ['Savings receive 0', 'verified', 'bc1qar0srrr7xfkvy5l643dfuqjyw2yr5w4tsrqfhg', \"m/84'/0'/0'/0/0\", '#0f6b45'],\n    ['Multisig deposit', 'verified', 'bc1qxy2kgdygjrsqtzq2n0yrf2493p83kkfjhx0wlh', \"m/48'/0'/0'/2'\", '#0f6b45'],\n    ['Exchange withdraw', 'external', 'bc1qw508d6qejxtdg4y5r3zarvary0c5xw7kv8f3t4', 'not derived here', '#8a6100'],\n    ['ETH contracts', 'verified', '0x8f2c41a7e0d5b93c6417ff08a2d9e1b74c0f5a63', \"m/44'/60'/0'/0/0\", '#0f6b45']\n  ],\n  vault: [\n    ['Bitcoin savings', 'unlocked', 'savings.cbx · 14.2 KB', 'Saved 13:58, verified by read-back.', '#0f6b45'],\n    ['Multisig records', 'locked', 'multisig.cbx · 9.7 KB', 'Saved 9 Aug, verified.', '#5c5344'],\n    ['Travel set', 'unsaved', 'travel.cbx · 4.1 KB', 'Never saved to a file. Download copies stay unverified.', '#b3261e'],\n    ['Device transfer', 'live only', 'animated QR · 42 frames', 'Nothing downloadable. The receiver enters the phrase itself.', '#8a6100']\n  ]\n};\n\nconst TABS = {\n  cold: [['⚒', 'Forge', 'forge'], ['∿', 'Derive', 'paths'], ['◈', 'Split', 'shares'], ['★', 'Secret', 'secret'], ['⊞', 'Hub', 'hub']],\n  warm: [['◱', 'Home', 'dashboard'], ['$', 'Money', 'portfolio'], ['R', 'Records', 'registry'], ['V', 'Vault', 'vault'], ['⚙', 'Set', 'settings']]\n};\n\nconst MORE = {\n  cold: [\n    ['P0.13', 'Vault session', 'unlock'], ['P1.1', 'Entropy Lab', 'entropy'], ['P1.3', 'Validate phrase', 'validate'],\n    ['P1.5', 'Child seeds', 'children'], ['P4.5', 'Passphrase Studio', 'passphrase'], ['P4.9', 'Descriptors', 'descriptors'],\n    ['P1.10', 'SeedQR studio', 'qr'], ['P2.7', 'Backup Health', 'backuphealth'], ['P4.3', 'Recovery Assistant', 'recovery'],\n    ['P4.4', 'Verify Bench', 'verifybench'], ['P1.7', 'Reveal hidden', 'conceal'], ['P1.7', 'Secret notes', 'notes'],\n    ['—', 'No secret yet', 'empty'], ['—', 'Lock & wipe', 'lock']\n  ],\n  warm: [\n    ['P1.8', 'Devices', 'devices'], ['P1.10', 'QR Studio', 'qrpublic'], ['P1.9', 'Address bench', 'addrbench'],\n    ['P3.1', 'Prices & FX', 'prices'], ['P3.9', 'Tax & exports', 'taxes'], ['P4.10', 'Reference', 'reference'],\n    ['P0.16', 'Verify this file', 'verifyfile'], ['P0.16', 'Provenance & legal', 'provenance'],\n    ['P0.17', 'Learn', 'learn'], ['all', 'Tool map', 'map'], ['✻', 'Enter sealed realm', 'hub']\n  ]\n};\n\nclass Component extends DCLogic {\n  state = { screen: 'hub', secret: 0, group: 'derive', scheme: 'slip39', revealed: false, more: false, settings: {}, qr: null };\n\n  go(id) { return () => this.setState({ screen: id, revealed: false, more: false, qr: null }); }\n\n  ent() {\n    return this.state.ent || { dice: [], coin: [], hex: [], cards: [], csprng: [], sim: {} };\n  }\n\n  addEnt(kind, val) {\n    const e = this.ent();\n    // CSPRNG is always the device RNG, so tapping it credits nothing.\n    const isDevice = kind === 'csprng';\n    this.setState({\n      ent: Object.assign({}, e, {\n        [kind]: (e[kind] || []).concat([val]),\n        sim: isDevice ? Object.assign({}, e.sim, { csprng: (e.sim.csprng || 0) + 1 }) : e.sim\n      }),\n      mixed: null\n    });\n  }\n\n  simEnt(kind, n) {\n    // Device-RNG values are recorded but earn no independent credit, which is\n    // the whole point of tracking them separately.\n    const e = this.ent();\n    const pool = M_SRC.filter(m => m[0] === kind)[0][3];\n    const add = [];\n    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) add.push(pool[Math.floor(Math.random() * pool.length)]);\n    this.setState({\n      ent: Object.assign({}, e, { [kind]: (e[kind] || []).concat(add), sim: Object.assign({}, e.sim, { [kind]: (e.sim[kind] || 0) + n }) }),\n      mixed: null\n    });\n  }\n\n  pill(on, fill) {\n    return 'flex:0 0 auto;padding:7px 12px;border:' + (on ? '3px' : '2px') + ' solid ' + (on ? '#000' : '#f4f0e2')\n      + ';border-radius:6px;background:' + (on ? (fill || '#ff007a') : '#1e1e2b') + ';box-shadow:' + (on ? '3px 3px 0 #000' : 'none')\n      + ';color:' + (on ? '#121212' : '#b3bcd4') + \";font-family:'Bangers',sans-serif;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase;font-size:14px;min-height:42px;white-space:nowrap\";\n  }\n\n  renderVals() {\n    const s = this.state;\n    const sc = SCREENS[s.screen] || SCREENS.hub;\n    const cold = sc.realm === 'cold';\n    const sec = SECRETS[s.secret];\n    const stocks = ['#fffdf5', '#e8f9ff', '#fff2f7'];\n    const group = GROUPS[s.group] || GROUPS.derive;\n    const scheme = SCHEMES[s.scheme];\n    const rows = ROWS[s.screen] || [];\n    const ent = this.ent();\n    const vTab = s.vTab || 0;\n    const vNamed = !!s.vNamed;\n    const vKdfPick = s.vKdfPick === undefined ? 1 : s.vKdfPick;\n    const mTarget = s.mTarget === undefined ? 4 : s.mTarget;\n    const mTargetBits = M_TARGETS[mTarget][0];\n    const mIndep = Math.min(mTargetBits, Math.floor(\n      M_SRC.reduce((sum, m) => sum + Math.max(0, (ent[m[0]] || []).length - (ent.sim[m[0]] || 0)) * M_BITS[m[0]], 0)\n    ));\n\n    const qrMods = [];\n    // Generated for the overlay AND for the SeedQR screen, which has no overlay\n    // — seeded from the focused secret so each secret gets a distinct pattern.\n    if (s.qr || s.screen === 'qr') {\n      const src = s.qr ? s.qr[1] : sec.fp + sec.label;\n      let h = 11;\n      for (let i = 0; i < 441; i++) {\n        h = (h * 1103515245 + src.charCodeAt(i % src.length) * 12345) % 2147483647;\n        const x = i % 21, y = Math.floor(i / 21);\n        const finder = (x < 7 && y < 7) || (x > 13 && y < 7) || (x < 7 && y > 13);\n        const ring = finder && (x % 7 === 0 || x % 7 === 6 || y % 7 === 0 || y % 7 === 6\n          || (x % 7 >= 2 && x % 7 <= 4 && y % 7 >= 2 && y % 7 <= 4));\n        const on = finder ? ring : (h % 100) > 47;\n        qrMods.push({ style: 'display:block;width:100%;aspect-ratio:1;background:' + (on ? '#121212' : '#fff') });\n      }\n    }\n\n    return {\n      guardDot: '#4ade80', guardShort: cold ? \"sealed · connect-src 'none'\" : 'warm · prices only',\n      toggleRealm: () => this.setState({ screen: cold ? 'dashboard' : 'hub', more: false }),\n      realmPill: 'flex:0 0 auto;padding:6px 11px;border:3px solid #000;border-radius:6px;background:'\n        + (cold ? '#ff007a' : '#00f0ff') + \";box-shadow:3px 3px 0 #000;color:#121212;font-family:'Bangers',sans-serif;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase;font-size:14px;min-height:44px;white-space:nowrap\",\n      realmLabel: cold ? '✻ Sealed' : '☼ Warm',\n      hazardStyle: 'display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;padding:4px 0;border-bottom:3px solid #000;background:'\n        + (cold ? 'repeating-linear-gradient(45deg,#ff007a 0 12px,#121212 12px 24px)' : 'repeating-linear-gradient(45deg,#00f0ff 0 12px,#121212 12px 24px)'),\n      hazardText: cold ? 'no network in here' : 'public data only',\n\n      showSwitcher: cold,\n      chips: SECRETS.map((x, i) => ({\n        label: x[0], fp: x[1], go: () => this.setState({ secret: i, revealed: false }),\n        style: 'flex:0 0 auto;display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:flex-start;justify-content:center;gap:1px;padding:6px 11px;border:2px solid '\n          + (s.secret === i ? '#000' : '#f4f0e2') + ';border-radius:6px;background:' + (s.secret === i ? '#00f0ff' : '#232331')\n          + ';box-shadow:' + (s.secret === i ? '3px 3px 0 #000' : 'none') + ';color:' + (s.secret === i ? '#121212' : '#b3bcd4') + ';min-height:44px'\n      })),\n\n      kicker: sc.kicker, kickerBg: sc.kickerBg, title: sc.title, lede: sc.lede,\n      hasCaption: !!sc.caption, caption: sc.caption || '', footNote: sc.foot,\n\n      isEntropy: s.screen === 'entropy',\n      mTargets: M_TARGETS.map((t, i) => ({\n        label: t[1],\n        go: () => this.setState({ mTarget: i, mixed: null }),\n        style: 'padding:8px 11px;border:' + (mTarget === i ? '3px' : '2px') + ' solid #121212;border-radius:6px;background:'\n          + (mTarget === i ? '#00f0ff' : '#fff') + ';box-shadow:' + (mTarget === i ? '3px 3px 0 #121212' : 'none')\n          + \";color:#121212;cursor:pointer;font-family:'Bangers',sans-serif;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase;font-size:14px;min-height:46px\"\n      })),\n      mBits: mIndep + ' / ' + mTargetBits + ' bits',\n      mBitsColor: mIndep >= mTargetBits ? '#0f6b45' : '#8a6100',\n      mBar: 'width:' + Math.min(100, Math.round(mIndep / mTargetBits * 100)) + '%;height:100%;background:'\n        + (mIndep >= mTargetBits ? '#4ade80' : '#ffde59'),\n      mBitsNote: mIndep >= mTargetBits\n        ? 'Full two-source protection. Even if the device RNG were compromised, this seed still has ' + mTargetBits + ' bits you produced yourself.'\n        : 'Keep going, or mix anyway and accept that the shortfall comes from the device RNG.',\n      mSources: M_SRC.map(m => {\n        const kind = m[0];\n        const log = (ent[kind] || []).slice(-14).join(kind === 'hex' ? '' : ' ');\n        const sim = ent.sim[kind] || 0;\n        const isDevice = kind === 'csprng';\n        // CSPRNG is counted in bytes drawn, not taps — each tap draws 32 or 64.\n        const amount = isDevice\n          ? (ent.csprng || []).reduce((n, v) => n + (parseInt(String(v).replace(/[^0-9]/g, ''), 10) || 0), 0)\n          : (ent[kind] || []).length;\n        return {\n          name: m[1],\n          count: amount + ' ' + m[2] + (sim && !isDevice ? ' · ' + sim + ' simulated' : ''),\n          log: log || 'nothing collected yet',\n          style: 'padding:13px 14px;border:3px solid #121212;border-radius:9px;background:' + m[4] + ';box-shadow:5px 5px 0 #000',\n          keys: m[3].map(k => ({\n            label: k,\n            go: () => this.addEnt(kind, k),\n            style: \"padding:10px 0;flex:1 1 44px;min-width:44px;border:2px solid #121212;border-radius:6px;background:#fff;box-shadow:2px 2px 0 #121212;color:#121212;cursor:pointer;font-family:ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace;font-size:14px;min-height:46px\"\n          })),\n          simNote: isDevice\n            ? 'always the device RNG · never earns independent credit'\n            : (sim ? sim + ' simulated · 0 credit' : 'device RNG · 0 credit'),\n          // A source that IS the device RNG has no meaningful \"simulate\" row.\n          genKeys: (isDevice ? [] : [10, 50]).map(n => ({\n            label: '+' + n,\n            go: () => this.simEnt(kind, n),\n            style: \"padding:8px 10px;border:2px dashed #8e8e9c;border-radius:5px;background:transparent;color:#5c5344;cursor:pointer;font-family:'Bangers',sans-serif;font-weight:400;font-size:13px;min-height:40px\"\n          }))\n        };\n      }),\n      mMixCopy: 'Mixing combines what you collected with fresh CSPRNG bytes. Simulated values are included but earn no independent credit.',\n      mMixBg: mIndep >= mTargetBits ? '#4ade80' : '#ffde59',\n      mMixLabel: mIndep >= mTargetBits ? 'Mix entropy' : 'Mix anyway',\n      mMixGo: () => {\n        const seedStr = (ent.dice.join('') + ent.coin.join('') + ent.hex.join('') + mTarget) || 'x';\n        let h = 2166136261, out = '';\n        for (let i = 0; i < mTargetBits / 4; i++) {\n          h = (h ^ (seedStr.charCodeAt(i % seedStr.length) || 61)) * 16777619 % 2147483647;\n          out += '0123456789abcdef'[Math.abs(h + i * 7) % 16];\n        }\n        this.setState({ mixed: out });\n      },\n      isQrScreen: s.screen === 'qr',\n      isVaultSession: s.screen === 'unlock',\n      vTabs: ['Manage', 'Create', 'Unlock'].map((t, i) => ({\n        label: t, go: () => this.setState({ vTab: i }),\n        style: 'flex:1 1 30%;padding:10px 8px;border:' + (vTab === i ? '3px' : '2px') + ' solid #121212;border-radius:6px;background:'\n          + (vTab === i ? '#ffde59' : '#fff') + ';box-shadow:' + (vTab === i ? '3px 3px 0 #121212' : 'none')\n          + \";color:#121212;cursor:pointer;font-family:'Bangers',sans-serif;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase;font-size:15px;min-height:48px\"\n      })),\n      vIsManage: vTab === 0, vIsCreate: vTab === 1, vIsUnlock: vTab === 2,\n      vVaults: [\n        ['savings.cbx', 'unlocked', '#4ade80', 'Steel plate · 12 records · saved 13:58', ['Lock', 'Rename', 'Save now']],\n        ['travel.cbx', 'locked', '#ffde59', '3 records · Argon2id moderate · saved 11 Aug', ['Unlock', 'Rename', 'Forget']],\n        ['legacy-2024.cbx', 'locked', '#ffde59', 'keyfile required · saved 3 Feb', ['Unlock', 'Rename', 'Forget']]\n      ].map(v => ({\n        name: v[0], state: v[1], stateBg: v[2], meta: v[3],\n        style: 'padding:13px 14px;border:3px solid #121212;border-radius:9px;background:'\n          + (v[1] === 'unlocked' ? '#e8f9ff' : '#fffdf5') + ';box-shadow:5px 5px 0 #000',\n        actions: v[4].map(a => ({\n          label: a,\n          style: 'flex:1 1 28%;text-align:center;padding:9px 6px;border:2px solid #121212;border-radius:5px;background:'\n            + (a === 'Unlock' ? '#00f0ff' : a === 'Forget' ? '#fff2f7' : '#fff')\n            + \";box-shadow:2px 2px 0 #121212;color:#121212;font-family:'Bangers',sans-serif;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase;font-size:13.5px;min-height:44px;display:block\"\n        }))\n      })),\n      vCreateBadge: vNamed ? 'Ready to create' : 'Name it first',\n      vFields: [\n        {\n          label: 'Vault name · public, stored unencrypted',\n          value: vNamed ? 'household-2026' : 'tap to name this vault',\n          border: vNamed ? '#0f6b45' : '#121212',\n          note: vNamed ? 'available — no other vault uses this name' : 'The name is how you tell vaults apart before unlocking, so it cannot be secret.',\n          noteColor: vNamed ? '#0f6b45' : '#5c5344'\n        },\n        {\n          label: 'Unlock phrase · six Diceware words or more',\n          value: vNamed ? '••••••••••••••••••••' : 'not entered',\n          border: vNamed ? '#0f6b45' : '#b9b0a0',\n          note: 'No strength score is invented from spelling or length. Length is what matters.',\n          noteColor: '#5c5344'\n        },\n        {\n          label: 'Confirm phrase',\n          value: vNamed ? '••••••••••••••••••••' : 'not entered',\n          border: vNamed ? '#0f6b45' : '#b9b0a0',\n          note: vNamed ? 'match' : 'A vault phrase typo is unrecoverable, so it is always confirmed.',\n          noteColor: vNamed ? '#0f6b45' : '#5c5344'\n        }\n      ],\n      vKdf: [['Interactive', '0.4 s'], ['Moderate', '1.4 s'], ['Sensitive', '4.1 s']].map((k, i) => ({\n        label: k[0], time: k[1],\n        go: () => this.setState({ vKdfPick: i }),\n        style: 'flex:1 1 30%;padding:9px 6px;border:' + (vKdfPick === i ? '3px' : '2px') + ' solid #121212;border-radius:6px;background:'\n          + (vKdfPick === i ? '#00f0ff' : '#fff') + ';box-shadow:' + (vKdfPick === i ? '3px 3px 0 #121212' : 'none')\n          + ';color:#121212;cursor:pointer;min-height:48px'\n      })),\n      vKdfNote: 'Measured here, not guessed — a phone is slower than a laptop, so the same profile costs more time.',\n      vCreateBg: vNamed ? '#4ade80' : '#8e8e9c',\n      vCreateLabel: vNamed ? 'Create vault' : 'Name it first',\n      vCreateNote: vNamed\n        ? 'Creates household-2026 and unlocks it. The name is written in the clear; everything else is encrypted with Argon2id and AES-256-GCM.'\n        : 'Tap the name field to see the flow with a name entered.',\n      vCreateGo: () => vNamed ? this.setState({ screen: 'empty', vTab: 0 }) : this.setState({ vNamed: true }),\n      vUnlockGo: () => this.setState({ screen: 'empty', vTab: 0 }),\n      mHealthBadge: mIndep >= 32 ? 'Health: pass' : 'Health: too little data',\n      mHealthBg: mIndep >= 32 ? '#4ade80' : '#ffde59',\n      mHealthStats: mIndep >= 32\n        ? 'chi-square p = 0.41 · runs: pass · lag-1 correlation 0.02'\n        : 'collect more before any test means anything',\n      mHasMix: !!s.mixed, mMixHex: s.mixed || '',\n      mMixMeta: (s.mixed || '').length * 4 + ' bits · ' + mIndep + ' independent + ' + (mTargetBits - Math.min(mIndep, mTargetBits)) + ' CSPRNG · raw key material',\n      mUseMix: () => this.setState({ screen: 'forge', revealed: false }),\n\n      isList: sc.kind === 'list', isWords: sc.kind === 'words',\n      isRows: sc.kind === 'rows' && s.screen !== 'entropy' && s.screen !== 'qr' && s.screen !== 'unlock',\n      isDeck: sc.kind === 'deck', isSettings: sc.kind === 'settings',\n\n      groupTabs: Object.keys(GROUPS).map(k => ({\n        label: GROUPS[k][0], go: () => this.setState({ group: k }), style: this.pill(s.group === k)\n      })),\n      tools: group[1].map((t, i) => ({\n        phase: t[0], title: t[1], note: t[2], ready: t[4] === 3 ? t[3] + ' · roadmap' : t[3],\n        tagBg: ['#00f0ff', '#ffde59', '#ff007a', '#4ade80'][i % 4],\n        readyColor: t[4] === 1 ? '#0f6b45' : t[4] === 2 ? '#8a6100' : '#5c5344',\n        go: this.go(t[5]),\n        style: 'display:block;width:100%;padding:13px 14px;border:3px solid #121212;border-radius:9px;background:'\n          + stocks[i % 3] + ';box-shadow:6px 6px 0 #000;min-height:44px'\n      })),\n\n      words: WORDS.slice(0, sec[2]).map((w, i) => ({\n        n: String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0'), t: s.revealed ? w : '••••••'\n      })),\n      wordKicker: s.screen === 'forge' ? 'Generated phrase' : 'Phrase · ' + sec[0],\n      wordPanel: 'padding:14px;border:3px solid ' + (s.revealed ? '#e02020' : '#121212')\n        + ';border-radius:9px;background:#fffdf5;box-shadow:6px 6px 0 #000;color:#121212' + (s.revealed ? '' : ';transform:rotate(-.4deg)'),\n      revealState: s.revealed ? 'REVEALED · 30 s' : 'masked',\n      revealColor: s.revealed ? '#b3261e' : '#5c5344',\n      toggleReveal: () => this.setState({ revealed: !s.revealed }),\n      revealBtnBg: s.revealed ? '#e02020' : '#ffde59',\n      revealBtnInk: s.revealed ? '#ffffff' : '#121212',\n      revealBtnText: s.revealed ? 'Hide now' : 'Reveal for 30 s',\n      revealNote: s.revealed\n        ? 'Straightened, no sticker, red border — §6 calm applies while words are on screen, on any size of display.'\n        : 'Masked by default. Pinch-zoom stays enabled, because zooming is how you check a word you just wrote down.',\n      facts: [\n        { k: 'Fingerprint', v: sec[1] },\n        { k: 'Words', v: sec[2] + ' · English' },\n        { k: 'Passphrase', v: 'set · confirmed' },\n        { k: 'Scope', v: 'cold realm only' }\n      ],\n\n      // Any row whose value is a public string a user might transcribe gets a\n      // QR. Same rule as desktop: if you can read it, you can scan it.\n      rows: rows.map((r, i) => {\n        const v = r[2];\n        const scannable = /^(bc1|0x|zpub|xpub|ypub|Zpub|npub)/.test(v);\n        return {\n          label: r[0], meta: r[1], value: v, note: r[3], hasNote: !!r[3], metaColor: r[4],\n          hasQr: scannable,\n          go: scannable ? () => this.setState({ qr: [r[0], v, r[3]] }) : null,\n          style: 'padding:12px 13px;border:3px solid #121212;border-radius:9px;background:' + stocks[i % 3]\n            + ';box-shadow:6px 6px 0 #000' + (scannable ? ';cursor:pointer' : '')\n        };\n      }),\n      qrOpen: !!s.qr,\n      closeQr: () => this.setState({ qr: null }),\n      qrTitle: s.qr ? s.qr[0] : '',\n      qrValue: s.qr ? s.qr[1] : '',\n      qrNote: s.qr\n        ? (s.qr[2] || 'Public. Scanning beats retyping — comparing the first and last few characters is the habit address-swapping malware relies on.')\n        : '',\n      qrModules: qrMods,\n\n      schemeTabs: Object.keys(SCHEMES).map(k => ({\n        label: SCHEMES[k][0], go: () => this.setState({ scheme: k }), style: this.pill(s.scheme === k, '#00f0ff')\n      })),\n      schemeCopy: scheme[1],\n      shareCards: scheme[2].map((holder, i) => ({\n        n: 'Share ' + (i + 1) + ' of ' + scheme[2].length, holder,\n        body: '•••••• ••••\\n••••• •••••••\\n••••••• ••••••',\n        style: 'flex:0 0 auto;width:158px;padding:12px 13px;border:3px solid #000;border-radius:8px;background:'\n          + stocks[i % 3] + ';box-shadow:5px 5px 0 #000;transform:rotate(' + ((i % 2 ? 1 : -1) * 1.1) + 'deg)'\n      })),\n\n      settingSections: SETTINGS.map((sect, si) => ({\n        title: sect[0], badgeBg: sect[1],\n        style: 'padding:14px;border:3px solid #121212;border-radius:9px;background:' + stocks[si % 3] + ';box-shadow:6px 6px 0 #000;color:#121212',\n        rows: sect[2].map((r, ri) => {\n          const chosen = s.settings[si + '-' + ri] === undefined ? r[3] : s.settings[si + '-' + ri];\n          return {\n            label: r[0], help: r[1],\n            options: r[2].map((o, oi) => ({\n              label: o,\n              go: () => {\n                const next = {};\n                Object.keys(s.settings).forEach(k => { next[k] = s.settings[k]; });\n                next[si + '-' + ri] = oi;\n                this.setState({ settings: next });\n              },\n              style: 'padding:7px 12px;border:' + (oi === chosen ? '3px' : '2px') + ' solid #121212;border-radius:6px;background:'\n                + (oi === chosen ? '#00f0ff' : '#fff') + ';box-shadow:' + (oi === chosen ? '3px 3px 0 #121212' : '1px 1px 0 #121212')\n                + \";color:#121212;font-family:'Bangers',sans-serif;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase;font-size:13.5px;min-height:44px\"\n            }))\n          };\n        })\n      })),\n\n      tabs: (cold ? TABS.cold : TABS.warm).map((t, i) => {\n        const on = t[2] === s.screen;\n        return {\n          icon: t[0], label: t[1], go: this.go(t[2]),\n          style: 'padding:9px 2px 11px;border-right:' + (i < 4 ? '2px solid #000' : '0') + ';background:'\n            + (on ? '#00f0ff' : 'transparent') + ';color:#121212;min-height:56px'\n        };\n      }),\n\n      moreOpen: s.more,\n      openMore: () => this.setState({ more: true }),\n      closeMore: () => this.setState({ more: false }),\n      moreItems: (cold ? MORE.cold : MORE.warm).map(m => ({\n        phase: m[0], label: m[1], go: this.go(m[2]),\n        style: 'display:flex;align-items:center;gap:9px;width:100%;padding:9px 10px;border:2px solid #121212;border-radius:7px;background:#fff;box-shadow:2px 2px 0 #121212;color:#121212;min-height:44px'\n      }))\n    };\n  }\n}\n\n<\u002Fscript>\n\n\n<\u002Fbody><\u002Fhtml>"
  </script>
</body>
</html>